 ```
 
+### ERA5 atmospheric forcing for MOM6/CICE
+
+For a regional ocean case using `CR_JRA` (or another `DATM%JRA` compset),
+CrocoDash can replace all eight JRA atmosphere streams with prepared ERA5
+fields.  `DATM%JRA` remains the CDEPS field interface, but no JRA atmospheric
+data are used in `full` mode.
+
+On NCAR systems, prepare the hourly RDA ds633.0 data and its ESMF mesh first:
+
+```bash
+python -m CrocoDash.raw_data_access.datasets.era5_atmos \
+  --start 2008-08-29T00:00:00 \
+  --end   2008-09-21T00:00:00 \
+  --output /glade/work/$USER/crocodile2026/era5_forcing/ike2008/era5_atmos_ike2008.nc \
+  --scrip  /glade/work/$USER/crocodile2026/era5_forcing/ike2008/era5_025_scrip.nc \
+  --mesh   /glade/work/$USER/crocodile2026/era5_forcing/ike2008/era5_025_ESMFmesh.nc
+```
+
+The atmospheric file contains `u10`, `v10`, `t2m`, `q2m`, `msl`, `precip`,
+`swdn`, and `lwdn`.  The helper uses ERA5 *mean-rate* products for
+precipitation and radiation; raw accumulated fields are not CDEPS-ready.
+Pass the resulting file and mesh in the same call that configures the rest of
+the case:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+
+force_dir = Path("/glade/work/faezehmaghso/crocodile2026/era5_forcing/ike2008")
+era5_file = force_dir / "era5_atmos_ike2008.nc"
+
+case.configure_forcings(
+    date_range=["2008-08-30 00:00:00", "2008-09-20 00:00:00"],
+    product_name="GLORYS",
+    function_name="get_glorys_data_from_rda",
+    # ... tides and other ocean inputs ...
+    era5_atmosphere_files={
+        field: era5_file
+        for field in (
+            "precip", "lwdn", "swdn", "q2m",
+            "msl", "t2m", "u10", "v10",
+        )
+    },
+    era5_mesh_filepath=force_dir / "era5_025_ESMFmesh.nc",
+    era5_atmosphere_mode="full",
+)
+```
+
+For the narrower wind/pressure sensitivity experiment used in the Hurricane
+Ike workshop notebook, set `era5_atmosphere_mode="wind_pressure"` and provide
+only `u10`, `v10`, and `msl`.  In that mode the other five streams remain JRA.
+After `case.setup --reset`, run `preview_namelists` and verify the generated
+`datm.streams.xml` references the ERA5 file in eight data-file entries before
+submitting the case.
+
 ## How to Check What's Required
 
 Before calling `configure_forcings()`, you can check what configuration options are required for your compset. It will also be printed on case initialization:
